================================================================================
PROJECT NOTICE — Finish Your Game Lab
================================================================================

Copyright (c) 2024–2026 finishyourgamelab, gogoapah.

This repository is the public companion to the YouTube channel
"Finish Your Game Lab" (https://www.youtube.com/@FinishYourGameLab).
It is a lab notebook of game-development prototypes, research notes,
and teaching material made for the channel's audience.

This notice is informational and is not itself part of the legal
license text. The binding legal terms are the unmodified license
texts reproduced in PART A and PART B below.

Dual licensing at a glance
--------------------------
This repository uses two standard licenses, depending on the kind of
material:

  * Source code (Lua, Python, the Lua/code portions inside .p8 files,
    shell scripts, build configs, and similar developer-authored
    code) is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License, including its
    standard non-endorsement clause. The full text is reproduced
    verbatim in PART A below.

      SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

  * Non-code material authored by the project (this README and other
    Markdown documentation, design notes, original artwork, original
    audio, and similar creative content) is licensed under the
    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY
    4.0). The full text is reproduced verbatim in PART B below.

      SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
      Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
      Full legal code:        https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

In short: you are welcome to fork, study, modify, and redistribute
the contents of this repository — including in your own commercial
games — as long as you keep the required attribution and respect the
non-endorsement clause. See PART A and PART B for the legally
binding terms.

Compilation / reservation of rights
----------------------------------
The authors regard this repository **as committed** — including its
curated directory layout, integration of components, selection of what
is checked in, file-level revisions, and testing — as embodying
substantial human creative choices. To the extent applicable law
recognizes copyright or related rights in that compilation,
coordination, or arrangement, those rights are asserted.

Rights **not** expressly granted under PART A (BSD 3-Clause) or PART B
(CC BY 4.0) remain **reserved**. Nothing in this notice waives,
assigns, or licenses trademarks except as each reproduced license may
require for lawful attribution.

Scope
-----
This dual-license arrangement applies to the entire Finish Your Game
Lab workspace repository — including all existing and future content
under paths such as `prototypes/`, `research/`, `tools/`,
`episodes/`, `docs/`, and `assets/` — unless a subdirectory
explicitly states otherwise (for example, by including its own
LICENSE file or a clear in-file notice).

Suggested attribution
---------------------
If you fork, modify, or redistribute material from this repository
(including incorporating it into your own commercial game), the
simplest way to satisfy the attribution requirements of both PART A
and PART B is to include something like the following in your
project's README, credits screen, or about page:

    Based on work by Finish Your Game Lab
    (https://www.youtube.com/@FinishYourGameLab).
    Original repository: <repo URL placeholder>
    Modifications: <briefly describe>
    Code portions licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
    Documentation and creative material licensed under CC BY 4.0.

You are free to phrase the attribution however is reasonable for
your medium (game credits, README, about box, etc.), as long as the
substance — author identification, license indication, and a link
back where reasonably practicable — is preserved.

Trademark / brand note
----------------------
"Finish Your Game Lab" is the name of a YouTube channel and an
informal brand identity used by the authors. The BSD 3-Clause
License's third condition (PART A, condition 3) and CC BY 4.0
Section 2(b)(2) and Section 2(a)(6) (PART B) already prohibit using
the channel name, the names of the authors, or any of their
brand identifiers to endorse, promote, or imply official sponsorship
of derivative works without prior written permission. Plain factual
attribution ("based on work by Finish Your Game Lab") is fine and
encouraged.

For licensing requests, sponsorships, written-consent enquiries, or
other business contact, please reach the channel via:

  https://www.youtube.com/@FinishYourGameLab

AI Disclosure
-------------
A large portion of the material in this repository was produced with
heavy AI assistance (so-called "vibe coding"): code, prose, design
notes, and some art/audio were drafted, expanded, or refactored by
generative AI under human direction.

Copyright law around highly automated or AI-assisted works is **still
evolving** and **fact-specific**. Regulators and courts continue to
address where human authorship begins and ends (see, for background
only, the U.S. Copyright Office materials on artificial intelligence
and related litigation such as *Thaler v. Perlmutter*). Other
jurisdictions take different approaches; consult qualified counsel if
the distinction matters for your project.

**Authors' position (informational, not legal advice):** the authors
consider the repository — files **as committed**, together with human
choices in prompting, iteration, selection among outputs, substantive
editing, refactoring, debugging, integration, and overall arrangement
— to reflect substantial human creative input for much of what is
distributed here.

Practical guidance for users of this repository:

  * The licenses in PART A (BSD 3-Clause) and PART B (CC BY 4.0) are
    granted **to the extent** the authors hold rights licensable
    under those instruments. They are intended to cover human
    creative contribution embodied in this work — including prompt
    design and iteration, curation and selection of AI outputs,
    integration, editing, refactoring, testing, arrangement, and the
    project viewed as a compilation — **without** the authors conceding
    the outer boundaries of protectability in every excerpt.

  * Whether any particular line, asset, or fragment might **later**
    be deemed outside copyright protection in some jurisdiction is
    **uncertain** and may depend on facts not visible from this
    repository alone. **Nothing in this disclosure** admits that any
    specific portion is unprotected, waives any claim the authors may
    have under applicable law, or invites reliance on informal
    summaries instead of PART A and PART B.

  * When you fork, copy from, or build on **material obtained from
    this repository**, comply with PART A and PART B (including
    attribution and non-endorsement) **unless** you have an
    independent legal basis to proceed otherwise. The authors
    **strongly encourage** the "Suggested attribution" example above
    for any reuse traceable to this project.

  * Nothing in this disclosure **expands or diminishes** the rights
    granted in PART A or PART B beyond what those license texts
    provide; it describes context and intent only.

